From 5bb10b560ae2ea9b7e9cd3d9df18e9859276a94a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:18:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(word): fit new inline pictures to the space at the
 insertion point

Inserted, pasted and dropped pictures were scaled to the width of the
section column only. In an indented paragraph (numbered exercise, list)
they overflowed the right margin, and in a table cell they widened the
column to the whole text width, reflowing the table and everything after
it. Their height was never limited, so a tall picture could exceed the
page.

Add CDocument.GetInlineObjectMaxSize (width of the current paragraph:
column, table cell, header or footer, minus its indents; height of the
column or cell) and FitInlineObjectSize (proportional scale-down to fit
both dimensions), and use them for Insert > Picture, image URLs, file
drag and drop, multi-image insertion and pasted pictures. This matches
Word, which fits a new picture into the text area at the insertion point.

[upstreamable]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
